<title>ITALY: Italy's Stet details 1996 cons results.</title>
<headline>Italy's Stet details 1996 cons results.</headline>
<text>
<p>ROME, May 9, Reuter - Year ending December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		    3,160    vs  2,452</p>
<p>    Cons pretax profit		 6,880    vs  5,781</p>
<p>    Tax charge			   3,720    vs  3,329</p>
<p>Profit before extraordinaries</p>
<p>			and tax	    7,278    vs  5,798</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   7,847    vs  7,212</p>
<p>    Gross operating margin	  20,194    vs 18,974</p>
<p>    Ord div			    130 lire   (unchanged)</p>
<p>    Savings share div		150 lire   (unchanged)</p>
<p>    Depreciation			10,742    vs 10,749</p>
<p>    Turnover			    40,522    vs 37,373</p>
<p>    Value added			 30,346    vs 28,809</p>
<p>    Labour costs			10,152    vs  9,835</p>
<p>    Net financial debt		12,040    vs 15,412</p>
<p>    Investments			 11,78     vs  9,072</p>
<p>Note - Stet is the Italian state telecommunications holding company and is in the process of being merged with state telecoms operator Telecom Italia.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
